        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Are Merach treadmills any good?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For walking, yes. The W50 TrekPad is a well-specified incline walking pad with a 400 lb rating and a published 1.25 HP continuous motor, and the T12 Pro offers 15% incline in a folding frame. None goes faster than 7.5 mph, so they are not running treadmills, and some published figures conflict, so buy on the lowest figure given.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where are Merach treadmills made?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Merach says it was founded in 2018 in Hangzhou, China, and its US store gives a registered address there. Its US support is by email and a US phone line, Monday to Friday, 8 AM to 8 PM Eastern.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does Merach give on treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One year on the frame and parts from delivery, plus an extra year if you register as a member on Merach’s site, for two years in total. The warranty page does not give separate motor terms, and does not say whether Amazon purchases qualify for the extra year, so ask Merach to confirm.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between the Merach W50 and W50 Lite?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The W50 TrekPad has a 1.25 HP continuous motor and a 400 lb rating; the W50 Lite has a smaller 0.75 HP continuous motor by independent figures, a 350 lb rating and 10% incline in its Amazon title, plus a Bluetooth speaker. Some retailer titles mix their figures, so check the model in the listing.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How fast does a Merach treadmill go?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The walking pads go 0.6 to 4 mph. The T12 Foldable, T12 Pro and T12 Aura go 0.5 to 7.5 mph. The T12 With Handles is listed both as 0.8 to 8.5 mph and 0.5 to 5.5 mph on the same page, so confirm its speed with Merach.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can I return a Merach treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Merach’s own store, within 30 days, undamaged and in its original packaging. You pay return shipping unless the item is defective or wrong, and defects must be reported within 24 hours with photos or video. Amazon orders follow Amazon’s return policy instead.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Merach W60 Plus rated for 400 lb?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sources disagree. Merach’s own page said 330 lb in November 2026, while Garage Gym Reviews and a walking-pad comparison site list 400 lb. Assume 330 lb until Merach confirms otherwise; the W50 TrekPad is the Merach with a consistent 400 lb rating.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
